TITLE:Rounds Spec
H1:M1 · Rounds (Day 2, Torres) <span class="draft">spec for approval</span>
SUB:Your first new kind of work: walk a route of machines, look at each one, and mark what you see. A worn machine you spot becomes a quick job "found by you", cheap now instead of a repair later. Step 2, sub-block 24a. From the plan's Part 2, M1 (<code>plans/pillar5-plan.md</code> v9); shared parts on <code>foundation.html</code>.
NAV:plain=In plain words|walk=Your first round|signs=What you see|grow=How it grows|crew=The crew|b=Builder|save=Save|tests=Tests|ranges=Builds and keys|faq=FAQ

<p class="note"><b>Approved by the lead (2026-10-18, overnight authority).</b></p>
<section id="plain">
  <h2>In plain words</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>The verb:</b> walk a route of 4-6 machines and <b>look</b> at each one (stand by it a moment; your character looks it over). You see a sign: "clean and quiet", "a faint rattle", "warm to the touch", "a drip under the pump". Then you <b>mark</b> it: <b>fine</b>, <b>worn</b>, or <b>something's off</b>.</li>
    <li><b>Why it matters:</b> a worn machine you mark gets a quick service job "found by you" (20 minutes, one part) instead of turning into a repair later. Something that's really going wrong gets its repair posted at once. That's prevention you can feel.</li>
    <li><b>No wrong answers that hurt:</b> mark a worn machine "fine" and nothing happens; the crew find it later, as now. Mark a fine one "worn" and Torres says "Looks all right to me." You get better at reading the signs; the Chief's notes and Torres's lines help.</li>
    <li><b>Where it lives:</b> a <b>round clipboard</b> (a Works datapad in your hand while you walk; the device shows the route). One round a morning, on the board as "Morning round, Deck 4".</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="walk">
  <h2>Your first round (Day 2, Tuesday)</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><time>Morning</time><b>Calder's first solo job</b><span>Pillar 4's Day 2 stays as it is: your first job alone with Calder (07:45).</span></li>
    <li><time>10:30, the Works tea corner</time><b>Torres finds you</b><span>"Fancy a walk? I'll show you my round." (A toast and the goal arrow; if you're busy, he waits for you at the Works bay until 11:30, then asks again after lunch.)</span></li>
    <li><time>The first two stops</time><b>He looks, you watch</b><span>Deck 4's round: Torres stops at the first washer, looks it over and says what he sees ("Hear that? Bearing's going. Worn."), marks it. The same at the scrubber.</span></li>
    <li><time>The rest</time><b>You look, he watches</b><span>He hands you the clipboard. You look at the next two or three and mark them; he says a word at each ("Good eye" or "Mm. Listen again").</span></li>
    <li><time>After</time><b>Trained</b><span>Any worn machine you marked is on the board, found by you. "Trained: rounds, with Torres." From Day 3 there's a morning round on the board each workday, held for you until 11:00.</span></li>
  </ol>
  <p class="note">Day 2 also has your first laundry after shift (0.60.7) and Rina's health check (14:00), so rounds is the day's only new thing.</p>
</section>

<section id="signs">
  <h2>What you see at each machine</h2>
  <p>A sign is chosen from the machine's real condition and kind; the same machine in the same state gives the same sign that day. Examples (the Works writer writes the full set, a few per kind and state):</p>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>State</th><th>Washer</th><th>Oven</th><th>Light relays</th><th>Air scrubber</th></tr>
    <tr><td>healthy</td><td>"Drum turns clean and quiet."</td><td>"Even heat, door seal snug."</td><td>"Steady light."</td><td>"A low, even hum."</td></tr>
    <tr><td>worn</td><td>"A faint rattle at the end of the spin."</td><td>"The door seal's a bit tired."</td><td>"A click now and then in the box."</td><td>"The hum's a touch higher than it should be."</td></tr>
    <tr><td>faulty and worse</td><td>"Water pooling under it."</td><td>"Hot one side, cool the other."</td><td>"The lights stutter."</td><td>"It's labouring; the air's stale near it."</td></tr>
  </table></div>
  <p class="note">The marks you can give are the same three everywhere. A worn machine is the one rounds are for: "something's off" on a faulty one also counts as found by you.</p>
</section>

<section id="grow">
  <h2>How it grows (only the first stage is on the main path)</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card"><b>Stage 1 · A set route</b><span>Each morning the clipboard gives a route of 4-6 machines on one deck (the decks take turns: 4, 3, 5).</span><span class="meta"><span class="tag">Day 2</span></span></div>
    <div class="card"><b>Stage 2 · Your own route</b><span>After 5 rounds you pick which machines to look at (5 of up to 9 on the deck). A well-picked round finds more; Torres notices ("You've got a nose for it").</span><span class="meta"><span class="tag">after 5 rounds</span><span class="tag new">optional</span></span></div>
    <div class="card"><b>Stage 3 · From the doorway</b><span>With the scanner (Day 5), you can read a room's machines from its doorway on your round: one look covers the room.</span><span class="meta"><span class="tag">with the scanner</span><span class="tag new">optional</span></span></div>
  </div>
  <p class="note">As you rise: as an Officer you choose any route (any deck you can enter); as a Senior Officer you also set the juniors' routes (the plan's job-by-rank map; built with Step 5).</p>
</section>

<section id="crew">
  <h2>The crew still do rounds</h2>
  <p>Today's crew inspection round (the <code>round</code> chore, 3 stops) keeps running. If you don't take your morning round by 11:00, it goes back to being a crew round, and they find worn machines as today. Nothing waits on you.</p>
</section>

<section id="b" class="builder">
  <h2>For the builder (seat M1, sub-block 24a)</h2>
  <h3>Sections touched</h3>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Section</th><th>What</th><th>Owner</th></tr>
    <tr><td>24a (new)</td><td><code>// 24a ROUNDS</code>: the route, the signs, the marks, the job kind, the ladder row's training</td><td>M1</td></tr>
    <tr><td>17</td><td>nothing new: 24a registers its kind with <code>jobKindAdd</code> (foundation 17.5) and posts found-by-you jobs with a new <code>machineFound(id, by)</code> (S adds it: sets <code>found</code> now on the machine's waiting service job, or posts it, and sends <code>simNote('found')</code>)</td><td>S (one function)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>15</td><td>the <code>look</code> step with <code>opts.marks</code> (foundation 15.1)</td><td>P</td></tr>
    <tr><td>8b</td><td>nothing: the clipboard is the <code>datapad</code> prop (<code>HOLDS.datapad</code>), held while a round job is yours and not done</td><td>—</td></tr>
    <tr><td>22 / content</td><td><code>content/works/signs.lines</code> (sign texts by kind and state), Torres's training lines (<code>train.m1</code>)</td><td>W</td></tr>
  </table></div>
  <h3>The job kind</h3>
  <div class="lines">jobKindAdd('rounds', { tier: 1, junior: false, work: 0,
  post: (h, jobs) =&gt; ...          // workdays at 07:00, once trained (SHIP.works.tr.m1): one round, held for you to 11:00
  stops: j =&gt; j.route.map(id =&gt; ({ deck, placeId: panelPlaceId(id), mins: 2, tag: 'look', how: 'look',
                                  opts: { marks: ['fine', 'worn', 'off'], sign: roundSign(id, day) } })),
  stepDone: (j, k, { pick }) =&gt; roundMark(j, k, pick),
  done: (j, t, by) =&gt; worksUse('m1'),
  crew: { can: p =&gt; p.work === 'work:works', mins: 25 } })</div>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Route</b> (stage 1): <code>roundRoute(day)</code>: the deck by <code>day % 3</code> (4, 3, 5; the training round is always Deck 4; skipping a deck with fewer than 4 machines with panel places), then 4-6 of its machines at your tier with <code>panelPlace</code>, ordered by a walk from the lift, picked with <code>schedU(day, 0, 860)</code>. Stage 2: the player picks with a <code>choose</code> step at the first stop (up to 9 shown, 5 picked).</li>
    <li><b>Signs:</b> <code>roundSign(id, day)</code> = a line from <code>signs.lines</code> for the machine's kind and <code>machineState</code> now, varied with <code>schedU(machSeed(id), day, 861)</code>.</li>
    <li><b>Marks:</b> <code>roundMark</code>: <code>worn</code> on a worn machine, or <code>off</code> on a faulty-or-worse one → <code>machineFound(id, 'you')</code>, xp +1 (foundation 24.4), the log's found-by-you flag. Anything else: nothing posted; a mark of <code>worn</code>/<code>off</code> on a healthy machine gets the teacher's (or the clipboard's) "Looks all right" line. Never a penalty.</li>
    <li><b>Held for you:</b> the round is held to 11:00 (<code>j.until</code>); then released to the crew (as <code>CHORES.round</code> does today). It never counts against <code>HOLD_MAX</code>.</li>
    <li><b>Training</b> (ladder row <code>m1</code>, foundation 24.2): Day 2, the ask at 10:35 (after the 10:30 tea); the teacher's round is the same kind with <code>j.train = 'm1'</code>, stops 1-2 done by Torres (<code>worksEscort</code> lead, he stands at the panel, his line plays), stops 3+ yours (<code>follow</code>).</li>
    <li><b>Stage 3:</b> once <code>hasTool('scanner')</code>, a stop's place may be the room's doorway (<code>roomDoorPlace</code>, or the nearest walkable tile inside the door) covering every machine in that room (one look, one mark each).</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="save" class="builder">
  <h2>Save</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The round is an ordinary job in <code>ship.jobs</code>, with <code>j.route</code> (machine ids) and <code>j.marks</code> (<code>{ id: 'fine'|'worn'|'off' }</code>).</li>
    <li>In <code>ship.works</code>: <code>use.m1</code>, <code>tr.m1</code> (foundation). Nothing else.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="tests" class="builder">
  <h2>Tests</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b><code>mech_check</code></b> (C's frame, the 24a part): a round posts service jobs for the worn machines you mark and nothing for healthy ones; found-by-you counted (xp, log); a round you don't take goes to the crew at 11:00 and they finish it; stage 2 opens after 5; the route and signs the same twice.</li>
    <li><b><code>career_check</code></b>: training on Day 2 with Torres for the steady player; asked again if missed.</li>
    <li><b><code>machine_check</code></b>: ship health unchanged (±1) with and without rounds over 14 days; the crew round still runs.</li>
    <li><b><code>intro_check</code></b>: Day 2's Pillar 4 beats unchanged (the solo job, the health check, the laundry).</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="ranges" class="builder">
  <h2>Builds and keys</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Seat <b>M1</b>, branch <code>claude/mech-rounds</code>, builds <b>0.45.x</b> (free, checked 2026-10-18).</li>
    <li>Hash keys <b>860-861</b> (route, sign variety).</li>
    <li>Merge after 24 core and 17.5 (<code>jobKindAdd</code>), and after <code>machineFound</code> in 17.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

